cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this report or its evidence, cite it as below."
title: "From GGUF to Native MLX: A Reproducible Fable Migration and the Memory Policy That Blocked It"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-25
license: MIT
type: report
abstract: >-
  A deployment engineering report on migrating the Qwen3.8-27B TURBO-Fable
  checkpoint from GGUF to a native MLX artifact on an Apple M4 Max with 64 GiB
  unified memory. It documents a bounded CPU-only conversion with full layout
  verification, four interleaved speculative-decoding conditions on an
  8,159-token prompt, two timed-out real agent repair sessions, and a
  serving-runtime system-memory guard whose documented switch converted a
  refused ~25k-token prefill into a completed reply. No 20 tok/s floor, ranked
  intelligence claim, peer review or near-limit context qualification is made.
